  "goodToKnow": "Der Zylinder is a cylinder, in geometry and in engines: ein Vierzylindermotor. It also means a top hat, from its shape, worn by chimney sweeps in their traditional costume and by magicians. Das Zylinderschloss is a cylinder lock, the standard in German doors. The Zy is pronounced tsü, stressed on the second syllable: tsü-LIN-der. From Greek kylindros (roller). Plural: die Zylinder."
